{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>Behind the tabernacle westward</b> — Scripture did not begin with the divisions of the Levites from the east, as it did with the banners, because there is no division of Levites there — only for Aaron and his sons the priests, and for Moses, who is the priest of priests. And it began from the west, which is the position opposite the east. But it placed in the south, which is more honored than it, the sons of Kohath, who are the most honored among the Levites, and it gave them the Ark and the Sanctuary. And in the west it placed the sons of Gershon, who is the firstborn, and it gave them the Tabernacle and the Tent. And it placed in the north, which is the remaining direction, the sons of Merari, and it gave them the furnishings of the Sanctuary."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:02:35.091251489Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}